  "title": "Knots that cross only held cuts are iterated 2-sums",
  "status": "Proved",
  "claim": "Knots that cross only held cuts are iterated 2-sums. In a knot space assembled along a tree of simple 3-edge cuts, after removing a line M: (1) every circuit of the solutions that crosses at least one cut, all of them held, is obtained from circuits that cross no cut by repeated 2-sums through the hubs of held cuts, (K1 - p) u (K2 - p') with K1 on a held cut's point side and K2 on its line side, each through one port; (2) every such iterated 2-sum is a circuit; (3) so a circuit that is not obtained this way crosses a cut that M opens: new emergence lives only across opened cuts. Proof: HUB-GLUE B at each held cut, by induction on the number of cuts crossed, using that in a tree every cut crossed by either part of a 2-sum is crossed by the whole. Checked as an exact set equality on the six assemblies of ticket A (all circuits) and on a chain of three Fano pieces (19 points, circuits up to 5 elements, one removal in each piece): 510 circuits crossing only held cuts, 162 of them across two held cuts at once, all iterated 2-sums.",
